    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "RAPL y Vampire: alcance de las mediciones",
      "type": "text",
      "datasource": null,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 5
      },
      "targets": [],
      "description": "",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "fixedColor": "#8F8F8F"
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": "/^Interna · RAPL/"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "#56A64B"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": "/^Externa · Vampire/"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "#FF9830"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": "/^Diferencia/"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "#5794F2"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "RAPL mide internamente los dominios energéticos de CPU disponibles. Vampire mide externamente la electricidad del servidor monitorizado. Sus alcances no son idénticos: la diferencia no se atribuye automáticamente a un componente concreto."
      }
    },
